From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Meyer zum Alten Borgloh <code@jzab.de>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:00:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] [pdx246] Add Sony Xperia 10 VI to fixup-mountpoints

Read from the phone (ls -l /dev/block/bootdevice/by-name/ under
LineageOS 23.2); it matches the GPT of stock firmware 70.2.A.4.168.
Bare names of slotted partitions map to slot a, as dhd's makefstab
ignores slotselect. The fstab uses block/by-name/ for metadata and misc,
so those are mapped under both prefixes.

The sed patterns are unanchored substrings, so the entries are sorted
longest path first: boot_b is replaced before boot, modemst1 before
modem.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I331efd7d900fa7aa76cbbf5b35dff43b89d8c939
---
